Built a stdlib-only `compress.py` that round-trips via `python3 compress.py corpus.txt out.bin` and `python3 compress.py --decompress out.bin restored.txt`. The program tries `zlib`, `bz2`, and high-preset `lzma`, stores the best payload with a tiny header, and verifies decompressed size on restore. Measured baseline `zlib.compress()` reduction was 88.7254%, while the implemented compressor achieved 93.3774% reduction on `corpus.txt` with byte-identical restoration (`cmp` succeeded). Registered a stable assay that returns 0 on any round-trip failure and otherwise prints the percentage reduction; it was accepted with median 93.3774 and zero spread. Tried several `compress.py` variants, but none outperformed the incumbent.